})();</script></div></div></div><div class="KLEmSd"></div><div data-encoded-docid="dPRSybtcRLtK-USyAAAAAA==" data-implicit-notification-eligible="false" data-result-index="0" data-title="Data Scientist + Gurobi (5+yrs)" role="group" jscontroller="leJiCf" jsdata="ZSBYQe;_;S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ449 xQKg9c;_;S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ450" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><div><div class="XFOJCe"><h2 class="HKvozf IFnjPb">Job description</h2><span jsname="QAWWu" class="OOyDTc">Location: Bangalore / Pune / Hyderabad<br>Experience: 5+ Years (can be adjusted as per requirement)<br>Employment Type: Contract / C2H (as applicable)<br><br>Job Overview<br><br>We are looking for a highly skilled Data Scientist with strong expertise in Mathematical Optimization and Gurobi to design and implement optimization models for complex business problems. The ideal candidate should have hands-on experience </span><span jsname="pqRzIf">...</span><span jsname="ij8cu" class="ejCXj" id="tsuid_S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ4_192" aria-live="polite" style="display:none">in Linear Programming (LP), Mixed Integer Programming (MIP), Operations Research, and Python-based optimization solutions. Experience in supply chain optimization and AWS cloud services will be an added advantage.<br><br>Key Responsibilities<br>• Design, develop, and optimize mathematical models using Gurobi (gurobipy).<br>• Build optimization solutions for Supply Chain, Scheduling, Routing, and Resource Allocation problems.<br>• Formulate and solve Linear Programming (LP) and Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) models.<br>• Perform data preprocessing, feature engineering, and analysis using Python, Pandas, and NumPy.<br>• Develop scalable optimization pipelines integrated with enterprise applications.<br>• Work closely with business stakeholders to translate real-world problems into optimization models.<br>• Automate model execution and workflows using Apache Airflow.<br>• Deploy optimization solutions on AWS using Lambda, AWS Batch, ECS Fargate, and Amazon SageMaker.<br>• Validate model performance and continuously improve solution quality and efficiency.<br>• Collaborate with cross-functional teams including Data Engineering, Analytics, and Product teams.<br><br>Required Skills<br>• Strong programming experience in Python.<br>• Hands-on expertise with Gurobi (gurobipy).<br>• Strong knowledge of Operations Research and Mathematical Optimization.<br>• Experience with Linear Programming (LP) and Mixed Integer Programming (MIP).<br>• Proficiency in Pandas, NumPy, SQL, and data preprocessing techniques.<br>• Experience in Supply Chain Optimization, Scheduling, or Logistics Optimization.<br>• Good understanding of optimization algorithms and modeling techniques.<br><br>Preferred Skills<br>• Experience with AWS Lambda, AWS Batch, ECS Fargate, Amazon SageMaker.<br>• Experience in workflow orchestration using Apache Airflow.<br>• Knowledge of cloud-based data pipelines and MLOps practices.<br>• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.<br><br>Qualifications<br>• Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Operations Research, Mathematics, Industrial Engineering, or a related field.<br>• 5+ years of experience in Data Science, Optimization, or Operations Research.<br>• Proven experience delivering optimization solutions in production environments.<br><br>Mandatory Skills<br>• Python<br>• Gurobi (gurobipy)<br>• Mathematical Optimization (LP/MIP)<br>• Operations Research<br>• Pandas &amp; NumPy<br>• SQL<br>• Data Preprocessing<br>• Supply Chain / Scheduling Optimization<br><br>Good to Have<br>• AWS Lambda<br>• AWS Batch<br>• ECS Fargate<br>• Apache Airflow<br>• Amazon SageMaker<br>• Cloud-based Optimization Deployment<br><br>Pay: ₹60,000.00 - ₹100,000.00 per month<br><br>Benefits:<br>• Provident Fund<br><br>Work Location: In person</span></div><div jsname="G7vtgf" class="TOQyFc Uzkg7d MmMIvd brKmxb" aria-controls="tsuid_S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ4_192" role="button" tabindex="0"