})();</script></div></div></div><div class="KLEmSd"></div><div data-encoded-docid="s0mZDPrZACiu-jxfAAAAAA==" data-implicit-notification-eligible="false" data-result-index="0" data-title="Data Scientist – AI Modelling (3 -5 years only)" role="group" jscontroller="leJiCf" jsdata="ZSBYQe;_;S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ469 xQKg9c;_;S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ470" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><div><div class="XFOJCe"><h2 class="HKvozf IFnjPb">Job description</h2><span jsname="QAWWu" class="OOyDTc">About the Role<br><br>The FCC DnA team is seeking an experienced Data Scientist to join our AI Modeling team and develop scalable Machine Learning, statistical and AI solutions.<br><br>This role is ideal for a hands-on Data Scientist who can independently translate business problems into modeling problems, evaluate multiple analytical approaches and recommend solutions based on data, statistical evidence and </span><span jsname="pqRzIf">...</span><span jsname="ij8cu" class="ejCXj" id="tsuid_S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ4_256" aria-live="polite" style="display:none">business requirements.<br><br>You will work across Statistical Modeling, Machine Learning, NLP and Generative AI while partnering with Product, Engineering and Business teams to take solutions from experimentation toward production.<br><br>We are looking for someone who goes beyond building a model and can clearly explain why a particular modeling approach was selected, how it was validated and what its limitations are.<br><br>Key Responsibilities<br><br>. Translate business problems and requirements into appropriate analytical and modeling approaches.<br><br>. Independently design, develop and evaluate statistical and Machine Learning models.<br><br>. Establish appropriate baseline and challenger models and objectively compare alternative approaches.<br><br>. Perform exploratory analysis, feature engineering, feature selection and data-quality assessment.<br><br>. Define appropriate model evaluation metrics based on the business problem and the cost of different types of errors.<br><br>. Apply cross-validation, hyperparameter tuning, out-of-sample testing and other robust validation techniques.<br><br>. Conduct detailed error analysis, sensitivity analysis and model diagnostics.<br><br>. Identify and address issues such as data leakage, class imbalance, multicollinearity, sampling bias and overfitting.<br><br>. Evaluate model explainability, stability and performance trade-offs.<br><br>. Clearly document model methodology, assumptions, limitations and validation results.<br><br>. Partner with Engineering and MLOps teams to transition models from experimentation into production.<br><br>. Support model monitoring, performance tracking and drift analysis after deployment.<br><br>. Build reusable modeling components and frameworks that can be leveraged across multiple use cases.<br><br>. Contribute to NLP, Generative AI, RAG and hybrid AI solutions where appropriate.<br><br>. Mentor junior Data Scientists and conduct code and model reviews.<br><br>. Communicate modeling recommendations and trade-offs effectively to business, Product and technical stakeholders.<br><br>Required Qualifications<br><br>Experience<br><br>. Approximately 3-5 years of hands-on experience in Data Science, Machine Learning, Statistical Modeling or Applied AI.<br><br>. Demonstrated experience independently developing and validating predictive models.<br><br>. Experience working across the model development lifecycle from data exploration through validation and productionization.<br><br>. Experience working with cross-functional Product, Engineering and Business teams.<br><br>Statistical &amp; Modeling Skills<br><br>. Strong understanding of statistical inference, probability, hypothesis testing and experimental design.<br><br>. Strong hands-on experience with regression, classification, tree-based models, ensemble methods and other Machine Learning techniques.<br><br>. Experience with algorithms such as logistic/linear regression, random forest, gradient boosting, XGBoost/LightGBM or comparable techniques.<br><br>. Strong understanding of feature engineering, feature selection and model diagnostics.<br><br>. Experience designing benchmark, baseline and challenger models.<br><br>. Strong understanding of model evaluation and the ability to select metrics appropriate to the business problem.<br><br>. Understanding of bias-variance trade-offs, sampling bias, class imbalance, data leakage and model stability.<br><br>. Experience with explainability techniques such as feature importance, SHAP or similar approaches.<br><br>. Ability to assess trade-offs between predictive performance, interpretability, complexity and maintainability.<br><br>Technical Skills<br><br>. Strong Python and modern Data Science ecosystem experience.<br><br>. Strong SQL and data manipulation skills.<br><br>. Experience developing production-quality, reusable modeling code.<br><br>. Familiarity with APIs and frameworks such as FastAPI.<br><br>. Familiarity with Git, Docker, CI/CD, cloud platforms such as Azure/AWS and MLOps practices.<br><br>. Experience with model deployment, monitoring and versioning is preferred.<br><br>. Experience with NLP, Generative AI, LLMs, embeddings, RAG or Agentic AI is desirable and will enable contribution across broader AI initiatives.<br><br>We Are Looking for Individuals Who<br><br>. Ask which modeling approach is most appropriate for the problem and can explain why.<br><br>. Challenge assumptions rather than automatically selecting the most complex algorithm.<br><br>. Are comfortable working with ambiguous business problems and defining a structured analytical approach.<br><br>. Balance experimentation with analytical rigor and production considerations.<br><br>. Take ownership of modeling workstreams and independently drive them to completion.<br><br>. Clearly articulate model performance, assumptions, limitations and business implications.<br><br>. Mentor junior team members and raise the quality of modeling practices around them.<br><br>. Collaborate effectively with Product, Engineering and business stakeholders.<br><br>. Remain current with developments across statistical modeling, Machine Learning and broader Applied AI.<br><br>Education<br><br>Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Engineering, Economics or another quantitative discipline.<br><br>Our Interview Practices</span></div><div jsname="G7vtgf" class="TOQyFc Uzkg7d MmMIvd brKmxb" aria-controls="tsuid_S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ4_256" role="button" tabindex="0" jsaction="EMtXr" data-l="" data-hveid="CCwQTQ" data-ved="2ahUKEwi5vuvUnIyYAxUkyzgGHS0dOOYQl5ACegQILBBN"><hr class="Bi9oQd" aria-hidden="true"><div class="Wjtive btku5b rXoM2c sjVJQd"><div class="niO4u VDgVie SlP8xc"><span class="cHaqb"><span class="PBBEhf">Show full description</span></span><span class="T2xY9b w2fKdd z1asCe" aria-hidden="true" style="height:18px;line-height:18px;width:18px"><svg focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960"><path d="M480-344L240-584l56-56L480-456L664-640l56,56L480-344Z"></path></svg></span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="XFOJCe" data-ved="2ahUKEwi5vuvUnIyYAxUkyzgGHS0dOOYQ5ZkFegQILBBO"><div class="EyBRub" data-ved="2ahUKEwi5vuvUnIyYAxUkyzgGHS0dOOYQyo8CegQILBBP"><div jscontroller="Wo3n8" jsname="aadvhe" jsmodel=" d5EhJe" data-bkt="horizon_jobs" data-fhs="" data-maindata='[null,null,"bind(&#39;java/com/google/gws/plugins/horizon/jobs/viewer/herocontent/jslayout/feedback_messages.html#JobAtEmployer&#39;,{employer_name:&#39;Wolters Kluwer India Private Limited&#39;,job_title:&#39;Data Scientist – AI Modelling (3 -5 years only)&#39;})","_S9P6avnsHqSW4-EPrbrgsQ4_257",null,13,null,null,null,null,null,5025273,"horizon_jobs",[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[["share_link","https://www.google.com/search?q\u003dData+Scientist+in+Pune+with+5+years+of+experience+jobs\u0